IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-registrar`
IMPORT `g4-council-membership`
IMPORT `g4-council-work`
IMPORT `g4-conflict`

-- g4-tests-red.l4: expectations that are MEANT TO FAIL.  Each one asserts, against the reading the encoding TOOK, the answer of the reading it
-- REJECTED at a fork (FRAGMENT-G4.md, section 2).  The module therefore fails once for each fork it covers, and that is how it proves that the
-- harness can fail.  There are 17 such assertions and all 17 must fail (check.sh names this file with expected_failed 17).
-- Each assertion's discriminating case is also asserted, in the right direction and against the alternative function, in the ordinary test module
-- of the section; nothing here is a defect.

§ `Expectations that the readings taken must not meet`

§§ `Cases`

seat2 MEANS `seat 2: the Registrar`
seat4 MEANS `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure`

`a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, no notice yet` MEANS `Appointment of a Registrar` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a foreign degree whose scope and content match` MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

`events: none` MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING
`events: a resignation on 2026-03-01` MEANS `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), NOTHING, NOTHING
`the Registrar appointed 2025-07-16` MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF "reg", seat2, (YMD 2025 7 16), 0, `events: none`, NOTHING
`a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 who resigned on 2026-03-01` MEANS `Service record of a member of the Council` OF "m4", seat4, (YMD 2025 7 16), 0, `events: a resignation on 2026-03-01`, NOTHING

`a member charged and later acquitted` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF (LIST (`Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` OF TRUE, `proceeding ended in a final judgment other than a conviction`)), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member barred by section 29(b)` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a member who ceased to be an employee of his ministry and so no longer satisfies the seat` MEANS `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` OF EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`an unjustified absence on` d MEANS `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF d, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`an attended meeting on` d MEANS `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF d, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` d MEANS `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` OF d, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

`absences in early 2024 and attendance in mid 2025` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 1 10), `an unjustified absence on` (YMD 2024 1 20), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2024 2 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 6 1), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 6 10), `an attended meeting on` (YMD 2025 6 20)
`three unjustified absences at subcommittee meetings` MEANS LIST `an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` (YMD 2026 1 10), `an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` (YMD 2026 2 10), `an unjustified absence at a subcommittee meeting on` (YMD 2026 3 10)

m1 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m1", TRUE
m2 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m2", FALSE
m3 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m3", FALSE
m4 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m4", FALSE
m5 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m5", FALSE
m6 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m6", FALSE
m7 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m7", FALSE
m8 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m8", FALSE
m9 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m9", FALSE
m10 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m10", FALSE
m11 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m11", FALSE

`eight serving, the chair among them` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7, m8
`all eleven serving` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7, m8, m9, m10, m11

`a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `eight serving, the chair among them`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`a meeting of three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m1", "m2"), (LIST "m3")
`a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-2, the chair and one other abstaining` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")

function2 MEANS `function (2): advising the Registrar on the Ministry's policy`
`advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure followed` MEANS `a subcommittee that advises the Council` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE)
`a consultation under (2), a subcommittee that followed the procedure` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function2, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure followed`)

`an employee of a private body that is the body represented` MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a member who is nobody's employee` MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the Gifts Law` MEANS `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`

§§ `The expectations that must fail`

-- RED 1, F-19a: publication is a condition of the appointment (the alternative reading says this person is not yet appointed).
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` `a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, no notice yet`

-- RED 2, F-19c-advice: consultation alone suffices (the alternative reading allows recognition once the Council was consulted, whatever became of its advice).
#ASSERT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE FALSE

-- RED 3, F-22-V: IL s.10(c) moves a Saturday end (2029-06-30) to Monday 2029-07-02; the reading taken does not apply it to a term.
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 1 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2025 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2029 7 2

-- RED 4, F-22-length: a further term of two years (the Minister fixes its length); the reading taken makes each further term four years.
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office when` 2 `terms of four years run from the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2031 7 16

-- RED 5, F-day: the day service ends counts as a day of service (a member who resigned on 2026-03-01 serves on 2026-03-01).
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2026 3 1) `according to` `a seat 4 member appointed 2025-07-16 who resigned on 2026-03-01`

-- RED 6, F-20-2: the Registrar's membership ends with the office (a Registrar whose office ended on 2026-03-01 does not serve on 2026-03-15; reading A: he serves until removed).
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2026 3 15) `according to` `the Registrar appointed 2025-07-16`

-- RED 7, F-23b1 (trap T29): s.23(b)(1) mirrors s.21, so a member charged and later acquitted is no ground for removal.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` `a member charged and later acquitted`

-- RED 8, F-23b3: the conditions "required for his appointment" are those of the seat only (the s.29(b) bar is not one of them).
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b)(3) — the member ceased to meet a condition required for the appointment` `a member barred by section 29(b)`

-- RED 9, C-23a-b3: the Minister's duty to remove arises even for a member who has already ceased to serve under s.23(a)(2).
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — the Minister's duty to remove the member arises` `a member who ceased to be an employee of his ministry and so no longer satisfies the seat`

-- RED 10, F-23c-year: "one year" is any year at all, or a calendar year (the reading taken uses the year ending on the day of removal, 2025-06-30).
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from more than half of the meetings of the Council held during the year ending on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `, among` `absences in early 2024 and attendance in mid 2025`

-- RED 11, F-23c-sub: meetings of a subcommittee are meetings of the Council.
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the member was absent without justification from three consecutive meetings of the Council` `three unjustified absences at subcommittee meetings`

-- RED 12, F-base: "its members" are the members serving (eight serving, five present with the chair: a quorum of five).
#ASSERT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair`

-- RED 13, F-T28: the Council may decide, not only deliberate, in an incomplete composition (three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1).
#ASSERT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1`

-- RED 14, F-25b-tie: a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal (a value, not a refusal): asserting a refusal of the alternative fails because it answers.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(b), alternative reading — a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal, at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-2, the chair and one other abstaining`

-- RED 15, F-26-sub: a subcommittee's delegated advice on function (2) is valid advice of the Council.
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (2), a subcommittee that followed the procedure`

-- RED 16, C-27: s.27(a) prevails over (b): a private-body employee who works for the body he represents is entitled to the travel refund.
#ASSERT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `an employee of a private body that is the body represented`

-- RED 17, F-28-scope: the status equation reaches the listed enactment whatever the act (an act outside the Council, under the Gifts Law).
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Gifts Law` `for an act in the Council being` FALSE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
